<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9608" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">com-plāno</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make even</i>, <i>level</i>, or <i>plain</i> (rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terram tabulā, manibus, pedibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 151, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montium juga,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Caes. 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opera, Auct. B. Alex. 63: domum,</span>”
				<i>to make even with the ground</i>, <i>to pull
					down</i>, <i>raze</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Dom. 38, 101</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">complanare et mollire aspera, dura,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to render tolerable</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Prov. 5, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
